        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on scope, success criteria, and initial backlog for the onboarding rollout.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 98050,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, welcome to the official channel for the Hybrid Customer Onboarding Workspace Rollout project. The main goal is to standardize our onboarding process for both online and in-office scenarios. Let's kick off by aligning on scope and how we'll measure success. I've started the initial task breakdown with T1 and T2. Please review the project brief when you have a moment.",
            "mentions": [
              14637,
              83011,
              95041,
              119847,
              387705
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "wave",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 119847,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks for setting this up! Quick question on scope: are we including the post-onboarding handover to the Customer Success team, or does this project end once the customer is fully set up?",
            "mentions": [
              98050
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 83011,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Hi everyone. What exactly is meant by 'hybrid'? Does that mean some people are in the office and some are remote during the same meeting?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 14637,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Good question. On that note, for the templates, should we also standardize internal project update emails, or focus only on customer-facing documents for now?",
            "mentions": [
              119847
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 98050,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Correct, it covers scenarios where our team or the customer's team might be split between office and remote. The process needs to work smoothly for both.",
            "mentions": [
              83011
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 98050,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Great points. To keep this manageable within the 21-day deadline, let's set some boundaries. I propose we define 'out of scope' as: 1) The formal handover process to CS (we'll ensure a clean handoff point, but not redesign their intake process) and 2) Internal-only project communications. Let's focus on customer-facing materials and the core workflow first.",
            "mentions": [
              119847,
              14637
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 387705,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "That makes sense. A clear scope will help us move faster. I'm good with that.",
            "mentions": [
              98050
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 14637,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "Agreed. That's a solid boundary for this phase.",
            "mentions": [
              98050
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 98050,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Perfect, decision D1 is locked in. Now for success metrics. The project brief mentions a pilot report with KPIs. I suggest we start by tracking 'Onboarding Cycle Time' and 'Number of Errors/Reworks'. I've asked for T12 to create a basic sheet for this.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 14637,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "From my past PM experience, separating 'errors' from 'rework' can be tricky. Could we combine them into a single 'Rework Events' metric? And maybe add 'Customer Satisfaction Score' from a simple post-onboarding survey? Just a thought.",
            "mentions": [
              98050
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 83011,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "How do we define cycle time? Is it from when the contract is signed?",
            "mentions": [
              98050
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 98050,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Good question. Let's define it as 'from project kickoff call to customer's formal acceptance of onboarding completion'. We can refine this in T2.",
            "mentions": [
              83011
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 98050,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "I like that simplification, 'Rework Events' is clearer. A customer survey might be out of scope for the initial pilot, but let's definitely keep it in mind for V2. So, for now, let's track: 1. Onboarding Cycle Time, and 2. Rework Events. This will be captured in A4. Does everyone agree?",
            "mentions": [
              14637
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
            "speaker_id": 119847,
            "reply_to": "M13",
            "text": "Works for me. Simple and measurable.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M15",
            "speaker_id": 14637,
            "reply_to": "M13",
            "text": "Sounds good. I can start drafting the A4 tracking sheet based on that. I'll take on T12.",
            "mentions": [
